  "result": "Excellent! All 326 tests pass. Here's a summary of the foreign currency implementation:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've added foreign currency support to `src/money.js` with three new components:\n\n### 1. **RATES** (exported constant)\nExchange rates relative to EUR:\n- `EUR: 1` (baseline)\n- `USD: 1.085` (1 euro = 1.085 dollars)\n- `GBP: 0.8425` (1 euro = 0.8425 pounds)\n\n### 2. **convert(eurCents, currency)** function\nConverts an amount from EUR cents to another currency.\n- Takes: amount in EUR cents, target currency code\n- Returns: `ok(amountInTargetCurrencyCents)` or `fail('UNKNOWN_CURRENCY')`\n- Uses `roundCents()` for precise rounding\n- Handles: positive/negative amounts, zero, large amounts\n\n**Examples:**\n- `convert(10000, 'USD')` \u2192 `ok(10850)` (100 EUR = 108.5 USD)\n- `convert(10000, 'GBP')` \u2192 `ok(8425)` (100 EUR = 84.25 GBP)\n- `convert(10000, 'JPY')` \u2192 `fail('UNKNOWN_CURRENCY')`\n\n### 3. **formatMoney(cents, currency)** function\nFormats currency amounts with appropriate signs.\n- `$` for USD: `$1,234.56`\n- `\u00a3` for GBP: `\u00a31,234.56`\n- `\u20ac` for EUR: `\u20ac1,234.56`\n- Includes thousands separators and 2 decimal places\n- Handles negative amounts: `-$2.50`\n\n### Error Handling\nAdded `UNKNOWN_CURRENCY` error code to `src/errors.js`:\n> \"Currency must be EUR, USD, or GBP.\"\n\n### Tests\n\nAdded **25 comprehensive tests** covering:\n- Exchange rate verification\n- Conversion to each supported currency\n- Rounding behavior (half-to-even)\n- Large and small amounts\n- Zero and negative values\n- Currency formatting with all currencies\n- Thousands separators\n- Invalid currency codes\n- Integration between `convert()` and `formatMoney()`\n- Precision preservation for common amounts\n\n**Total: 326 tests pass** (301 existing + 25 new for currency conversion)",
